#====================================================================
# DRAFT-gtk2-legacy-frontend — GTK+2 时代 GUI 前端库在仅有 GTK3 包的
#   仓库中的系统性阻塞:pc 别名只能过 configure,过不了编译
# 触发事件: xsane 0.999 HarmonyOS PC 适配(前置适配轮)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-gtk2-legacy-frontend (corroborates E348)
trigger_tool:           configure|pkg-config|make|clang
phase:                  configuration|compilation
error_signature:        No package 'gtk\+-2\.0' found|
                        Package 'gtk\+-2\.0'.*not found|
                        'GtkObject' undeclared|
                        unknown type name 'GtkObject'|
                        'GdkGC' undeclared|
                        'GtkTooltips' undeclared|
                        storage size of.*isn't known

severity:               2
category:               platform, compat, dependency, autotools, gtk
match_keywords:         gtk+-2.0, gtk+-3.0, GTK2, GTK3, alias pc, pc alias,
                        GtkObject, GdkGC, GdkPixmap, GtkTooltips, GdkInputCondition,
                        GtkSignalFunc, AM_PATH_GTK_2_0, pkg-config probe,
                        xsane, GTK 2-era, source port, fail-fast, validate()

title:                  GTK+2-era frontends: a gtk+-2.0 pc alias can pass configure but cannot make GTK3 headers compile

root_cause: >
  Legacy GUI frontends written against GTK+ 2 hard-code a pkg-config probe for
  gtk+-2.0 (often via AM_PATH_GTK_2_0) and use GTK 2-only API surfaces. When the
  repository only ships a GTK 3 package, a generated gtk+-2.0.pc alias that
  Requires: gtk+-3.0 (technique corroborated by E348) satisfies configure-time
  version and cflags/libs probes, but the source still references types removed
  in GTK 3 (GtkObject, GdkGC, GdkPixmap, GtkTooltips, GdkInputCondition,
  GtkSignalFunc). Compilation then fails in src/*.c against GTK 3 headers. The
  gap is an API/ABI generation gap, not a probe problem: no recipe-level alias
  can bridge it.
affected_scope: >
  Any repository package that upstream-probes gtk+-2.0 and calls GTK 2-only
  APIs while the repo provides only gtk/3.x (observed on xsane 0.999 where 9+
  src/*.c files use the removed types). Also applies to GTK+ 1.2 fallback
  paths (AM_PATH_GTK) and to configure-only green builds that hide the real
  compile failure until make.

verification_cmd: >
  pkg-config --modversion gtk+-2.0;
  grep -lE 'GtkObject|GdkGC|GdkPixmap|GtkTooltips' src/*.c;
  if any hits, expect compilation failure despite a successful configure.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           fail-fast-validate-plus-split-dependency
rec_description: >
  Do not ship a recipe that is known to fail mid-compile. In the consuming
  package, raise ConanInvalidConfiguration in validate() for the affected
  profile (os=OHOS) listing the concrete missing GTK 2 APIs, and record the
  blocked status in manifest.yaml and notes. Track the real fix as a separate
  GTK+ 2 dependency adaptation (its own issue/branch/PR) or an explicitly
  scoped GTK 3 source port of the frontend; do not smuggle either into the
  consuming package's PR. Keep the gtk+-2.0 pc alias in the recipe so the
  moment a GTK 2 package lands, configure and the rest of the recipe are
  already correct.
rec_command: >
  conan create archives/x/xsane/0.999 -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<ohos-profile>
  --build="xsane/*"  # expected: validate() fails fast with the GTK 2 blocker
  message until gtk2 exists
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-validate-guard

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      gtk2-package-then-re-enable
fallback_description: >
  After a GTK+ 2 package is adapted and merged, remove the validate() guard,
  point the gtk+-2.0 alias/probe at the real package, and re-run device
  validation end to end.
fallback_command:       ""
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          dependency-follow-up

forbid_1_pattern:       alias-only-fix (ship gtk\+-2\.0 alias without validate guard)
forbid_1_reason:        The alias makes configure green and defers failure to a confusing mid-compile error, wasting device CI time.
forbid_1_consequence:   A blocked package enters build queues and fails with errors far from the root cause.

forbid_2_pattern:       vendor.*gtk.*2\.\d+.*source (vendoring GTK 2 sources into the consumer PR)
forbid_2_reason:        Dependency adaptations belong in their own issue/branch/PR per the one-library-one-PR constraint.
forbid_2_consequence:   Review-unable PR mixing a toolkit port with a frontend package.

forbid_3_pattern:       status:.*built|passed.*when.*compile.*failed
forbid_3_reason:        Recording a configure-pass as a build success misrepresents the validation state.
forbid_3_consequence:   Downstream consumers trust a package that never produced a binary.

principles:             P016
similar_to:             E348
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-gtk2-legacy-frontend.md
last_updated:           2026-09-12
source_event:           archives/x/xsane/0.999

authors:                codex
source_pr:
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  0
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.8
metrics_last_used:      2026-09-12
